conventional utterance like "Good Night", why not just use a relevant utter=
ance=20
and make a convention about it.  Loglan had 'speni lo gudbi'  (which was=20
probably eventually something else) "Experience good things". Note it is no=
t an=20
imperative nor a hortative or the like, just a bare form floating around, j=
ust=20
the sort of thing for a conventional utterance.  Of course, you have to=20
translate it over and maybe dress it up for particular occasions (Good Nigh=
t,=20
Happy Birthday, etc.) but the general pattern has been around for 55 years =
now. =20
why diddle?


